{
  "summary": "P1 lost laptop (KB-021). User Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, mei.chen@brightline.example) reports leaving work laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) in an Uber last night; unsure whether it was locked. Device status: ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11T02:39:51Z (Sat Oct 10 ~21:39 Chicago), no warnings. Since it is online, a remote lock/wipe should reach it quickly. Please remotely lock and/or wipe it. Sign-in logs (14 days): 10 successful sign-ins, all Chicago, all Duo push, residential/corporate networks, normal hours. Nothing suspicious so far and nothing since 10/09. Account active, VPN enabled. Data at risk: Operations/logistics work data, cached M365 mail (mailbox is at 99.4%, about 50 GB, likely cached locally), and saved VPN/M365 sessions. Action taken: block_sign_in queued for technician approval. Still needed: approve the block, remote lock/wipe, password reset once identity is verified by phone, revoke sessions/tokens, and a replacement device. User was asked to contact Uber lost & found and to file a police report if it looks stolen.",
  "reason": "KB-021 says always escalate lost devices for remote lock/wipe; P1."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for telling us so fast. We're treating this as urgent. We've asked a technician to block sign-ins to your account so nobody can use the laptop to get into your work account. Once that's approved, you won't be able to sign in either until we reset your password. We'll call the phone number we have on file to confirm it's you and give you a new password. Our senior support team has your case and can lock or wipe the laptop remotely. In the meantime: 1) Report the lost item in the Uber app (Help > Report an item you lost) and contact the driver. 2) If it looks like the laptop was stolen, please file a police report and send us the report number. 3) Reply with roughly when and where you last had it, and whether you remember locking it or closing the lid. If you get it back, let us know right away so we don't wipe it.",
  "internal_note": "P1 lost device, KB-021. User_id 9, laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15). It is ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11T02:39:51Z (about 21:39 Chicago on 10/10). Sign-in logs (14 days) look clean: all Chicago, Duo push, usual hours, and nothing since 10/09. Account active, VPN enabled. Mailbox at 99.4% (about 50 GB), so cached mail on the device is likely. Queued block_sign_in (approval_id 1) because the device may be unlocked and in someone else's hands. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1) for remote lock/wipe. Next steps: approve the block, lock/wipe while the device is online, verify identity by phone and then reset the password, revoke sessions, and provide a replacement laptop. Asked the user when and where it was last seen and whether it was locked, and told them to file a police report if stolen.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-021"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
